/-!
# Etale descent of local module flatifications

Source: Stacks Project, `flat.tex`, Tag 0814, lemma `lemma-flatten-module-etale-localize`
(blueprint: lem-trf-etale-flattening-descent).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- Etale local flatifications of a quasi-coherent module are dominated by one admissible
blow-up of the base.

Source: Stacks Project, `flat.tex`, Tag 0814, lemma `lemma-flatten-module-etale-localize`
(blueprint: lem-trf-etale-flattening-descent).
The hypotheses encode a quasi-compact and quasi-separated base `S`, a quasi-coherent module
`F` on `X`, a quasi-compact open `U`, and a finite jointly surjective family of diagrams
`Xi --j i--> X`, `Xi --g i--> Si --e i--> S` commuting with `f`.  Each `e i` is
quasi-compact and etale, each `j i` is etale, and both families cover their targets.  For
each `i`, the given `e i ⁻¹ᵁ U`-admissible blow-up `B i` makes the strict transform of
the pullback of `F` along `j i` flat over `B i`.  The conclusion supplies a `U`-admissible
blow-up `B` of `S` whose strict transform of `F` is flat over `B`.

The proof follows the ten steps of the Stacks Project argument. (1) Refine each `S i` by a
finite affine open cover and restrict `X i`; quasi-compactness, etaleness, covering, and the
local flatness hypotheses are preserved by these restrictions and by flat base change. (2) For
an arbitrary admissible blow-up `b : S₁ ⟶ S`, base change the two covering families to
`T i := S i ×_S S₁` and `Y i := X i ×_S S₁`; etale covering base change and the blow-up
flat-base-change comparison preserve the hypotheses and identify the pulled-back transforms.
(3) Blow up `T i` in the extension of the given local centre. The product-ideal comparison and
the admissible-blow-up calculus compare the two orders of blowing up; the transform which is
flat by hypothesis stays flat after the second blow-up and agrees with the transform in the
other order. (4) Choose a finite-type quasi-coherent ideal with zero set `S \ U`, principalize
it by a preliminary blow-up, and pass to finitely many affine charts on which the resulting
Cartier ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor. (5) On one affine chart `S = Spec A` with
`U = D(a)`, refine every `S i` by finitely many affine opens. For each resulting etale affine
map `A ⟶ B`, apply the etale ideal factorization to write the local centre as
`I B_g = (J B_g) J'` with `V(I) ⊆ V(a)`; retain finitely many such principal neighborhoods.
(6) Reindex the finite refinement by `r`, set `I = ∏ r I r` (the empty product is `A`), and
blow up `S` in `I`. Its pullback to each `S r` factors as the given local blow-up followed by
the blow-up of the remaining factor, and the successive centres have the same support as the
product centre. (7) On each pullback `S r ×_S S^b`, the local transform is flat by the
admissible-blow-up calculus and agrees with the pullback of the global transform by strict
transform base change. (8) The maps from these pullbacks are etale, flat, and jointly
surjective. Stalkwise transitivity of flatness therefore makes the global transform flat over
`S^b`, and descent along the jointly surjective source family gives flatness on
`X ×_S S^b`. (9) Extend the finitely many affine-chart solutions to admissible blow-ups of the
whole preliminary base, blow up the product of their centre ideals, and use the same product
comparison, strict-transform calculus, and finite affine cover to glue them. (10) Compose the
glued blow-up with the preliminary boundary blow-up; the calculus shows that the composite is
`U`-admissible and its transform is the flat transform constructed above. Empty schemes and
the empty finite product are covered by the vacuous and unit-ideal cases, and `U = S` gives
the unit-centre case.
-/
theorem exists_admissibleBlowup_moduleStrictTransform_isFlatOver_of_finite_etale_cover
    {S X : Scheme.{u}} [CompactSpace S] [QuasiSeparatedSpace S]
    (f : X ⟶ S) (F : X.Modules) [F.IsQuasicoherent]
    (U : S.Opens) (hU : IsCompact (U : Set S))
    {ι : Type v} [Finite ι]
    (Si : ι → Scheme.{u}) (Xi : ι → Scheme.{u})
    (g : ∀ i, Xi i ⟶ Si i) (j : ∀ i, Xi i ⟶ X) (e : ∀ i, Si i ⟶ S)
    (hcomm : ∀ i, g i ≫ e i = j i ≫ f)
    (he_qc : ∀ i, QuasiCompact (e i)) (he_etale : ∀ i, Etale (e i))
    (hj_etale : ∀ i, Etale (j i))
    (he_cover : ∀ s : S, ∃ i : ι, ∃ x : Si i, e i x = s)
    (hj_cover : ∀ x : X, ∃ i : ι, ∃ y : Xi i, j i y = x)
    (B : ∀ i, IsAdmissible (Si i) ((e i) ⁻¹ᵁ U))
    (hB_flat : ∀ i,
      letI : (B i).I.toModules.IsFiniteType :=
        (B i).I.isFiniteType_toModules_sheaf (B i).finiteType
      Scheme.Modules.IsFlatOver
        (@Scheme.Modules.moduleStrictTransform (Xi i) (Si i) (g i) (B i).I
          inferInstance ((Scheme.Modules.pullback (j i)).obj F) inferInstance)
        (pullback.snd (g i) (B i).I.blowupMap)) :
    ∃ B' : IsAdmissible S U,
      letI : B'.I.toModules.IsFiniteType :=
        B'.I.isFiniteType_toModules_sheaf B'.finiteType
      Scheme.Modules.IsFlatOver
        (@Scheme.Modules.moduleStrictTransform X S f B'.I inferInstance F inferInstance)
        (pullback.snd f B'.I.blowupMap) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
